WEBVTT

00:06.820 --> 00:09.570
<i>There's so many books on design...</i>

00:09.820 --> 00:10.530
<b>Brr Brr</b>

00:10.770 --> 00:12.730
<i>Crap, I gotta get going.</i>

00:10.780 --> 00:11.780
Alarm

00:14.730 --> 00:16.240
<i>I'll have to continue this later.</i>

00:16.500 --> 00:18.620
<i>This summer break, I'm going to study a lot,</i>

00:18.620 --> 00:20.970
<i>absorb the knowledge, and 
improve my sense of style.</i>

00:21.430 --> 00:24.910
<i>I really need to find my own strengths soon.</i>

00:25.670 --> 00:26.420
<b>Wander</b>

00:28.290 --> 00:29.000
<b>Wander</b>

00:31.090 --> 00:35.010
<b>Forgot where to 
return the books to.</b>

02:05.470 --> 02:09.980
<b>#19 
New Member</b>

02:06.060 --> 02:07.800
So after all that at the library,

02:08.250 --> 02:10.800
I spent so long looking for
 the right shelf that it made me late.

02:11.050 --> 02:12.070
I'm sorry!

02:12.070 --> 02:12.950
You're late.

02:13.450 --> 02:16.450
If you take your books to the front desk, 
they'll return them for you.

02:16.450 --> 02:17.830
Wait, really?

02:18.960 --> 02:21.440
I'll go get the tickets.

02:19.740 --> 02:22.700
<b>The Lost Diary</b>

02:21.440 --> 02:21.890
Okay.

02:21.890 --> 02:22.690
Okay.

02:23.250 --> 02:26.540
So this movie is based on 
a book Hayate-san likes?

02:26.540 --> 02:28.100
I think so.

02:28.100 --> 02:30.370
I heard Mima-san was in charge 
of that huge advertisement

02:30.370 --> 02:32.230
they put up at Shinjuku Station.

02:32.230 --> 02:33.240
My older brother told me.

02:33.710 --> 02:36.050
He's really good at his job, huh.

02:36.050 --> 02:36.850
He really is.

02:36.850 --> 02:39.270
How cool are people who 
are good at their jobs?

02:40.150 --> 02:42.850
I can't wait to be one of those people, too.

02:43.950 --> 02:45.050
Thanks for waiting.

02:45.780 --> 02:47.200
Is any seat fine for you?

02:47.200 --> 02:47.780
Yeah.

02:47.780 --> 02:49.550
Hey, let's get some drinks.

02:49.550 --> 02:50.750
I'm going to the restroom.

02:50.750 --> 02:52.500
Can you get me a ginger ale?

02:52.500 --> 02:53.330
Got it.

02:54.530 --> 02:57.880
We'll have a ginger ale, a lemon drink, and..

02:57.880 --> 02:58.790
I'll take a cola.

02:58.790 --> 03:00.040
A cola.

03:00.040 --> 03:01.600
Is that everything for you?

03:01.600 --> 03:02.060
That's it.

03:02.510 --> 03:04.360
Here you go.

03:04.360 --> 03:05.770
Thank you.

03:06.860 --> 03:08.000
So that reminds me.

03:08.770 --> 03:10.900
I guess you go to the library too, huh?

03:11.250 --> 03:12.540
Do you like books?

03:11.500 --> 03:17.250
Look of "I found 
a kindred spirit"

03:12.540 --> 03:14.330
A normal amount.

03:14.330 --> 03:17.260
<i>I mean, I haven't been to a 
library in like 10 years...</i>

03:17.690 --> 03:18.740
I'm back.

03:18.740 --> 03:19.710
What are you talking about?

03:20.020 --> 03:21.550
The library.

03:21.550 --> 03:22.270
Here you go.

03:22.270 --> 03:22.790
Thanks.

03:23.270 --> 03:25.100
The library, huh.

03:25.100 --> 03:27.520
It's a little too quiet for me in there.

03:27.770 --> 03:28.390
<b>Slurp</b>

03:29.410 --> 03:30.680
This is cola.

03:30.680 --> 03:32.140
And this?

03:33.760 --> 03:35.490
No, that's lemony.

03:35.490 --> 03:36.430
Then this is it.

03:36.440 --> 03:37.400
<b>Sip</b>

03:37.780 --> 03:38.660
Yeah.

03:39.210 --> 03:40.660
Keep it straight, man.

03:40.660 --> 03:42.850
It's because you took so long.

03:43.110 --> 03:46.040
A group of guys, all friends, sharing drinks.

03:45.870 --> 03:47.490
<b>Peace</b>

03:46.040 --> 03:47.450
They do look close.

03:49.960 --> 03:51.510
You ever sit down at the movies

03:51.510 --> 03:53.540
and find yourself looking for the seatbelt?

03:53.840 --> 03:55.200
Totally.

03:54.790 --> 03:55.250
<b>Miss</b>

03:58.450 --> 04:00.990
The book this movie is based 
off of is also really good.

04:00.990 --> 04:02.030
I hope you read it.

04:02.030 --> 04:02.590
Okay.

04:02.720 --> 04:05.170
<i>Am I the only one who 
thought that was funny?</i>

04:05.300 --> 04:07.390
<b>Turn it OFF in the theater!</b>

04:05.540 --> 04:08.250
I don't read books, like, ever.

04:08.250 --> 04:10.690
Are the book and the movie 
really that different?

04:11.000 --> 04:12.950
They have to condense an entire 
book down to two hours,

04:12.950 --> 04:14.360
so of course there's going to be changes,

04:14.360 --> 04:18.400
but it can happen that the movie adaptation 
turns out really fun in its own right!

04:18.400 --> 04:19.560
Really?

04:19.560 --> 04:21.020
He's so lively now.

04:21.020 --> 04:23.060
I mean, I haven't seen it yet either,

04:23.060 --> 04:24.800
so I don't know how the movie's going to be.

04:24.800 --> 04:28.020
It would be funny if you were mad 
as hell the second it's over.

04:28.020 --> 04:29.120
That's not going to happen.

04:29.380 --> 04:30.860
I see.

04:30.860 --> 04:32.950
I guess we're all seeing the 
movie for the first time,

04:32.950 --> 04:35.060
but you're a fan of the original work, too.

04:35.060 --> 04:35.860
Yeah.

04:35.860 --> 04:39.340
But seeing the advertisement
 Mima-san worked on

04:39.340 --> 04:41.470
made me really excited about the movie.

04:42.590 --> 04:44.330
Oh, it's starting.

04:44.330 --> 04:48.190
It's amazing to be able to make
 a fan of the original say that.

04:53.190 --> 04:53.970
That...

04:54.230 --> 04:55.690
<b>Sigh</b>

04:54.350 --> 04:55.760
That was so good!

04:56.170 --> 04:58.830
The end made me cry a bit too.

04:58.830 --> 05:01.870
I did not think the ending 
would be that moving.

05:01.870 --> 05:02.820
That was fun.

05:02.820 --> 05:04.870
I'm going to go buy a program.

05:04.870 --> 05:06.770
Okay. We'll wait right here.

05:07.300 --> 05:09.860
I wonder how it differed 
from the original.

05:10.300 --> 05:11.910
Maybe I should read the book too.

05:12.220 --> 05:14.760
I'll just have Hayate-san tell me.

05:14.760 --> 05:17.280
There's no way I'd ever finish reading it.

05:17.280 --> 05:17.870
Huh?

05:18.270 --> 05:19.140
Hey.

05:19.870 --> 05:20.690
Over there.

05:21.120 --> 05:21.830
What?

05:26.000 --> 05:27.460
A girl's picking him up!

05:27.830 --> 05:30.750
Hayate-kun's good looking and kind of meek,

05:30.750 --> 05:34.290
so girls get carried away by summer
 break vibes and try to pick him up!

05:34.290 --> 05:37.930
All while he's looking like he doesn't 
know the first thing about women.

05:37.930 --> 05:41.400
He sure seems happy about it, though.

05:41.850 --> 05:44.030
It's like he's the girl.

05:48.260 --> 05:51.230
Wait, isn't that...?

05:51.460 --> 05:51.960
<b>At the park...</b>

05:51.750 --> 05:52.000
<b>That day</b>

05:51.960 --> 05:52.000
<b>At the park...</b>

05:52.000 --> 05:52.040
<b>That day</b>

05:52.000 --> 05:53.370
<b>At the park...</b>

05:52.040 --> 05:53.370
<b>That day</b>

05:54.400 --> 05:57.710
Wait, you're the original author 
of the movie we just saw?!

05:57.710 --> 05:59.070
Nice to meet you.

05:59.080 --> 05:59.800
Pant

05:59.480 --> 06:02.260
I just heard it too. It was very shocking.

05:59.800 --> 06:00.550
Pant

06:00.580 --> 06:01.340
<b>Squeeze</b>

06:00.590 --> 06:01.310
Pant

06:01.340 --> 06:02.010
Pant

06:02.260 --> 06:04.830
Wait, aren't you Takayuki's friend?

06:04.830 --> 06:05.980
Huh? Yeah.

06:05.980 --> 06:08.190
You saw that movie?

06:08.190 --> 06:08.960
What?

06:08.960 --> 06:10.190
<i>Is he involved in the project?</i>

06:10.520 --> 06:12.130
I wrote the book.

06:10.640 --> 06:12.100
<b>Thank you!</b>

06:12.390 --> 06:14.060
<b>Slam</b>

06:13.360 --> 06:14.130
That's what happened.

06:14.810 --> 06:17.700
Now my heart won't stop hammering.

06:17.700 --> 06:19.140
Huh.

06:19.770 --> 06:20.840
<i>Wow.</i>

06:21.210 --> 06:23.670
<i>When people's skills synergize,</i>

06:23.670 --> 06:25.740
<i>you get this kind of outcome.</i>

06:28.740 --> 06:30.330
Do you all know each other?

06:30.330 --> 06:32.970
I don't want to get in the 
way, so I'll get going.

06:32.970 --> 06:34.080
Oh, sure.

06:34.670 --> 06:37.870
Next time, we need to hang out properly.

06:34.700 --> 06:35.410
<b>Tug</b>

06:37.870 --> 06:42.380
<b>Sweet Sweet</b>

06:38.160 --> 06:39.980
Yup, I promise.

06:39.980 --> 06:41.480
Don't forget!

06:41.480 --> 06:42.530
Bye-bye!

06:43.470 --> 06:45.930
You don't need to go with your girlfriend?

06:45.930 --> 06:47.750
She isn't my girlfriend.

06:48.390 --> 06:50.880
Just an old friend I randomly met.

06:50.880 --> 06:53.570
<i>I guess popular authors get the girls.</i>

06:53.810 --> 06:56.370
You're Takayuki's friends, right?

06:56.870 --> 06:59.070
I'm Igarashi Motoharu.

06:59.070 --> 06:59.770
It's nice to meet you.

07:00.050 --> 07:02.290
Takayuki... You mean, Mima-san?

07:02.290 --> 07:03.420
You're friends?

07:03.420 --> 07:05.600
I thought you were just work acquaintances.

07:05.600 --> 07:07.560
I knew him a long time ago.

07:07.560 --> 07:09.240
But he did also do a great 
job with that assignment.

07:09.560 --> 07:10.730
Oh, yeah,

07:10.730 --> 07:14.210
do you know a cafe where you can hang
 out without worrying about the time?

07:14.210 --> 07:15.900
I just moved to Tokyo.

07:15.900 --> 07:17.590
My older sister has a nice cafe.

07:17.590 --> 07:18.610
It's a hidden gem.

07:18.610 --> 07:19.570
Oh, where is it?

07:19.570 --> 07:20.460
Is it on the map?

07:20.460 --> 07:25.790
<b>Friendly  Friendly</b>

07:20.460 --> 07:25.790
<b>Just like that, they're friends</b>

07:20.820 --> 07:23.570
I don't think it's on the 
map, but it's around here.

07:23.570 --> 07:25.790
Hey, we should all go together.

07:25.790 --> 07:32.970
Badump badump

07:26.620 --> 07:29.930
So you're the owner's brother and her employee?

07:27.220 --> 07:30.150
<i>How are they just talking to 
him like he's a normal person?</i>

07:30.300 --> 07:32.970
<b>Nerd at 














his limits</b>

07:30.350 --> 07:33.050
The French toast is really good there.

07:33.640 --> 07:35.510
Shiki Souta is my older brother.

07:35.510 --> 07:39.230
Oh, really? He was also 
really easy to talk to.

07:39.710 --> 07:43.010
I feel like I've been blessed with 
the people around me, I really do.

07:43.420 --> 07:45.700
And they did such a great 
job on the movie, too.

07:46.430 --> 07:47.550
<i>Oh, right.</i>

07:47.550 --> 07:50.150
<i>Here's someone who created 
something from nothing.</i>

07:51.530 --> 07:52.360
What is it?

07:52.680 --> 07:53.890
Oh, nothing.

07:54.460 --> 08:00.080
I was just wondering how one cultivates 
the ability to charm people like you do.

08:01.040 --> 08:03.500
<b>Blunt</b>

08:01.610 --> 08:03.020
It comes when you get it out.

08:03.020 --> 08:05.800
Huh? What does that mean?

08:03.490 --> 08:05.800
Hayate-san, shouldn't you take 
this opportunity to talk to him?

08:06.090 --> 08:07.470
I can't...

08:10.960 --> 08:11.970
<b>Stare</b>

08:15.490 --> 08:19.480
You have the eyes of someone who's
 itching to start doing something.

08:19.970 --> 08:22.670
Why don't you just start, 
instead of overthinking it?

08:22.670 --> 08:25.470
Your sense of style develops through action.

08:26.080 --> 08:29.770
Get a part of yourself out that 
even you don't know about.

08:29.770 --> 08:31.200
That's where it all begins.

08:31.640 --> 08:33.900
That's what I mean by, "it 
comes when you get it out."

08:35.100 --> 08:36.260
What are you talking about?

08:36.260 --> 08:36.940
The toilet?

08:36.940 --> 08:37.490
Yep.

08:37.490 --> 08:38.120
No, we're not!

08:38.380 --> 08:40.600
So, Hayate, which college do you go to?

08:40.600 --> 08:42.000
Hayate?! My name?!

08:40.790 --> 08:43.590
<i>I always thought I needed to 
have my unique strengths...</i>

08:42.000 --> 08:43.580
Oh, was that not it?

08:43.710 --> 08:48.550
<b>What are my unique strengths?</b>

08:44.190 --> 08:46.780
<i>Could it be that my problem 
isn't that I don't have them,</i>

08:46.780 --> 08:48.370
<i>but that I'm not using them?</i>

08:50.630 --> 08:53.560
<i>Your sense of style develops through action.</i>

08:56.600 --> 08:57.500
Asami-san!

08:57.900 --> 09:02.730
If you ever have another project like the 
help-wanted flyers, please let me do it.

09:03.040 --> 09:04.860
Even if it's something small.

09:04.860 --> 09:05.900
Sure.

09:05.900 --> 09:07.820
If something comes up, I'll let you know.

09:08.200 --> 09:09.440
Thank you.

09:09.440 --> 09:12.800
Souma, can you come over
 here so I can take a picture?

09:12.800 --> 09:13.730
A picture?

09:14.510 --> 09:20.620
<i>The eyes of someone itching to start
 doing something are so pretty.</i>

09:21.040 --> 09:24.870
<b>Igarashi Motoharu</b>

09:21.040 --> 09:24.870
<b>Igarashi Motoharu</b>

09:21.040 --> 09:24.870
<b>Your cute friends are all mine now</b>

09:21.460 --> 09:24.880
<i>Your cute friends are all mine now.</i>

09:25.600 --> 09:26.830
When did this happen?

09:27.470 --> 09:29.010
<i>Give them back.</i>

09:28.830 --> 09:29.340
<b>Send</b>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.980
<b>Coming up next</b>

10:59.970 --> 11:04.980
<b>Things You Don't Like</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

11:04.980 --> 11:09.970
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
